infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Sticky sessions vs externalized state
  desc The same goal — keep the session alive — two architectures
  compares
    - label Sticky sessions (affinity)
      children
        - label 1.5–2.5x load imbalance
          desc Pinned clients cannot be rebalanced
        - label Session is a SPOF
          desc Pinned backend crash loses 100% of that session, no failover
        - label LB must pin every request
          desc Cookie or IP hash; routing is constrained
        - label Workaround, not a solution
          desc Hides stateful backend design
    - label Externalized state (Redis)
      children
        - label Any backend can resume
          desc Session lives in Redis, not one backend's memory
        - label Survives backend failure
          desc Crash is invisible to the user
        - label LB routes freely
          desc Power-of-two-choices, no affinity needed
        - label Netflix, Airbnb, Shopify
          desc The horizontal-scaling default
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
